question:
In the Cartesian coordinate system, the origin coincides with the pole of the polar coordinate system, and the positive $x$-axis is the polar axis. The line $l$ passes through the point $P(-1,1)$, and its slope angle is $\alpha=\frac{5\pi}{6}$. The polar equation of the curve $C$ is $\rho=4\sin\theta$.
(I) Find the parametric equation of line $l$ and the Cartesian equation of curve $C$;
(II) Suppose line $l$ intersects curve $C$ at points $A$ and $B$. Find the value of $\overrightarrow{PA}\cdot\overrightarrow{PB}$.
